,"severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.679cfcddd2bb5871197dfd101de29be63bb4d4a7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.679cfcddd2bb5871197dfd101de29be63bb4d4a7.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 3:46PM MDT until October 26 at 9:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is ongoing\n\n* WHERE...Western Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthern San Juan County in southeastern Utah...\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 AM MDT Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along San Juan River is occurring. Low-water\ncrossing are inundated with water and may not be passable. The\nriver is running fast and high. Do not attempt to cross.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 342 PM MDT, The San Juan River is forecast to crest tonight\naround midnight between Bluff and Mexican Hat. A second rise and\nhigher crest is forecast along the San Juan River, peaking at\nMexican Hat Sunday Monday.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nSan Juan River\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMexican Hat, Tselakai Dezza, Bluff, Halchita, Montezuma Creek and\nAneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-26T09:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3a13c08d00e9f0eaecf417945ed4320e5cfecd7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3a13c08d00e9f0eaecf417945ed4320e5cfecd7.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 11:59AM MDT until October 25 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is imminent or ongoing with additional rounds of showers\nand thunderstorms expected through Saturday afternoon. Rivers and\ncreeks may still experience high waters even after rainfall has\nended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a28b19253bb7550e7a42b701dae47ec9af4c8ee0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a28b19253bb7550e7a42b701dae47ec9af4c8ee0.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-24T05:07:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 240507 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1107 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flooding is ongoing across portions of southeast Utah and southwest Colorado, and is expected to continue through Saturday. - While some rivers have crested, some rivers will experience their crest Saturday. - Isolated to scattered showers and storms are ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-24T04:45:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is